course: dictionary
lesson: 11088
title: Wetland: wet land full of life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wetland is an area of land that is wet all or much of the year, or covered with shallow water. You can work out the meaning from the context. «Wetlands such as marshes and swamps soak up flood water like a sponge.» The sentence tells you that the land holds water, so a wetland must be a wet place.
explain: The word is built from two smaller words: wet and land. Wet land is a good clue, and it matches the meaning. Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «Wet land such as marshes and swamps soak up flood water like a sponge.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Marshes, swamps and bogs are all kinds of wetland. «The Pantanal in Brazil is the world's biggest tropical wetland, where jaguars hunt caimans.» Here the wetland is a huge home for big animals, so it is a place where wildlife lives, not just a wet patch of ground.
fact: A wetland is land that is wet, or covered with shallow water, for much of the year.
fact: Marshes, swamps and bogs are all kinds of wetland.
fact: Wetlands are homes for many birds, frogs, fish, insects and plants.
fact: Wetlands clean water like a filter and soak up floodwater like a sponge, which helps protect towns.
fact: Many wetlands have been drained for farms and buildings, so they are now protected.
exercise: What is a wetland? | A busy town square | *An area of land that is wet or covered with shallow water for much of the year | A dry, sandy desert | A tall mountain covered in snow
exercise: Which of these is NOT a kind of wetland? | Bog | *Desert | Marsh | Swamp
exercise: «Wetlands such as marshes and swamps soak up flood water like a sponge.» What does soak up mean? | Freeze solid | Make a loud noise | *Take in and hold | Throw away
test: «Many wetlands have been drained for farms and buildings.» What does drained mean here? | Filled with rain | Frozen in winter | Painted bright blue | *Had their water removed
test: Wetlands are home to many birds, frogs and fish. Which animal is most likely to live in a wetland? | Polar bear on the ice | *Frog in a marsh | Camel in the desert | Shark in a mountain lake
exam: Why are wetlands important? | They are always dry and sandy | They are used only for building roads | They make the rain stop | *They clean water, soak up floodwater and are homes for many animals and plants
